          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"148\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This misuses the MCU's internal-regulator bypass pins and exposes the VCAP nodes on the UART connector, potentially preventing correct MCU operation and risking damage or unreliable communication.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC1", "NAVC1", "HSE1", "HSE2"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "FCC crystal connections go to PE6 (pin 5) and PE7 (pin 37), not the MCU's PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. NAVC's crystal and load components are not connected to NAVC1; its PH0 and PH1 pins instead connect to separate capacitor-to-ground nets.",
      "expected": "Each MCU's HSE crystal circuit should connect between its HSE input and output pins (PH0/PH1 on these parts), with the associated load components.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"HSE_OUT_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R32\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has the specified external crystal correctly connected, so operation using the intended HSE clock will fail or be unreliable.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected, the FCC's VCAP pins are wired to UART3 connector nets, and neither MCU's HSE crystal circuit is correctly connected. Any one of these defects would materially prevent the intended board behavior."
}

